"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[7004],{73986:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"init","desc":"Creates `ServerStorage.TestHook` in Studio. Does nothing on a live server.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":158,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/TestHookService.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"TestHookService","desc":"Studio-only test hook for the playtest scenarios in `tests/scenarios/`. In\\nStudio it creates a `BindableFunction` named `TestHook` under\\n`ServerStorage`; on a live server it creates nothing. There is no remote,\\nso only server code, the command bar and the Studio MCP exec VM can call\\nit. The MCP exec VM can\'t see game module state, which is why the hook\\nexists: its callback runs in the game\'s own VM.\\n\\n`ServerStorage.TestHook:Invoke(command, args)` returns `(ok, result)`:\\n\\n| Command | Args | Does |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `grant` | `{ userId, coins?, xp?, itemId?, quantity? }` | credits through [CurrencyService] / [InventoryService] |\\n| `read` | `{ userId, paths? }` | profile values as JSON (the whole profile without `paths`) |\\n| `nextGame` | `{ gameMode, map }` | queues the next round\'s mode and map |\\n| `forceRoles` | `{ Murderer = { userId }, Sheriff = { userId } }` | roles for the next Murder Escape round |\\n| `paidRandomItems` | `{ userId, restricted? }` | overrides the paid random items verdict; `nil` clears it |\\n| `largeServer` | `{ players? }` | player count that brings a second Sheriff; `nil` resets it |\\n| `ownPasses` | `{ userId, passes }` | gameplay pass names (`GamePassData`) the active round treats as owned |\\n| `setPity` | `{ userId, boxId, count }` | sets the player\'s crate pity counter (`box_pity[boxId]`) |\\n| `receipt` | `{ userId, productId, purchaseId?, price? }` | runs the game\'s receipt handler with a fake receipt; returns the decision name |\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":29,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/TestHookService.luau"}}')}}]);